From 45afaa06538c00f422d255ae5f824d0b0bf51d7c Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: t <tristan75015@gmail.com>
Date: Mon, 12 Oct 2026 06:55:09 +0200
Subject: [PATCH] CuDSSSolver: fixes of an independent review

- the decision to create a new solver of MFEM is collective: the layout of
  the matrix (local numbers of rows and columns, global number of rows,
  first row) and, with ReuseAnalysis, its pattern are compared on all
  processes, all of them taking part in the reduction (a process keeping
  its local size skipped it, and a process keeping its local size while
  the global layout changed kept the descriptors of the previous layout);
- the operator must be a HypreParMatrix (the SparseMatrix path of MFEM is
  wrong with a communicator);
- when hypre computes on the host, MFEM gives cuDSS host arrays through a
  copy between device arrays: the solver is refused unless the GPU reads
  the pageable memory of the host;
- cuDSS does not report the failures of the factorization, which give
  wrong solutions, finite or not: each solution is checked by its
  relative residual (1e-3), computed on the device, and a failure is
  reported by hasConverged;
- the pattern of a matrix stored on the device is compared without
  reading its values: its index arrays are copied into buffers allocated
  when the pattern is recorded (HypreMatrixPatternRecord), nothing being
  allocated before the collective reduction;
- documentation: requirements (CUDA-aware MPI on several processes,
  hypre on the host), failures reported or stopping the program, failures
  of the distributed analysis of cuDSS 0.7.1;
- DirectSolverReuseAnalysisTest: a step moving a row between processes
  (three processes, the layout of the first process being kept), a step
  adding rows to the last process, a negative definite matrix declared
  positive definite (failure reported), variants on three processes and
  with hypre on the host, and the refusal tested without the device
  configured by the environment.

Six mutations of the cuDSS solver and of the pattern record are detected
(collective decision short-circuited, no pattern comparison, no residual
check, pattern forgotten after a reuse, buffers not copied, global
indices of the off-diagonal columns not compared).
